<title>MEXICO: SOCCER-MEXICO BEAT ST VINCENT 5-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-MEXICO BEAT ST VINCENT 5-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico beat St Vincent 5-1 (halftime 2-0) in a CONCACAF semi-final stage group three World Cup qualifying match on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Mexico - Benjamin Galindo (20th and 28th, penalty), Zague</p>
<p>(48th), Carlos Hermosillo (72nd), Dexter Walker, own goal (81st)</p>
<p>St Vincent - Kendall Velox (88th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Mexico	    4  3  0  1 12  4  9</p>
<p> Jamaica	   4  2  1  1  7  3  7</p>
<p> Honduras	  4  2  1  1  6  5  7</p>
<p> St Vincent	4  0  0  4  3 16  0</p>
<p>Note: top two go through to the final CONCACAF qualifying</p>
<p>stage.     </p>
<p>Next match: Nov 6 - Mexico v Honduras</p>
</text>
